			"12": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": true
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "CAMERA 2D\n\nThe Camera 2D node constructs a Camera2D type that can be used on the Render 2D and Shape Render nodes.\n\nThe Camera can be panned by applying a transformation and zoomed by sending a float signal to the zoom inlet.\n\nThe scale parameter scales the lens, essentially you are scaling yourself!\nThe bigger the scale, the smaller the image.\nThis parameter also allows you to flip the image by using a negative scale value.\n\nBy default the camera will adhere to the aspect ratio, but this can be changed to absolute mode where you can manually set the bounds of the camera using the Box2D type."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 310.70989990234375,
					"width": 600.81591796875,
					"x": 36.62862014770507812,
					"y": 221.3148956298828125
				},
				"class": {
					"id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
					"version": 1
				},
				"clock": "video",
				"color": "ffd0c117",
				"constants": {},
				"hidden": [
					"text",
					"alignment",
					"font-size",
					"fill"
				],
				"name": "Comment",
				"thumbnail_visible": true
			},
			"13": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": false
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "EXAMPLE 1: BASIC CAMERA\n\nThis example demonstates the basic use of the Camera 2D node by exposing the zoom and transformation inlets and creating sliders for them."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 709.6983642578125,
					"width": 1200.926025390625,
					"x": 37.11753463745117188,
					"y": 561.48797607421875
				},
				"class": {
					"id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
					"version": 1
				},
				"clock": "video",
				"color": "ff02bbff",
				"constants": {},
				"hidden": [
					"text",
					"alignment",
					"font-size",
					"fill"
				],
				"name": "Comment",
				"thumbnail_visible": true
			},
			"16": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": false
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "EXAMPLE 3: ABSOLUTE\n\nIn this example we are using the Camera2D node in absolute mode.\nWhen we enable this in the node panel, we are no longer using the aspect ratio, but are allowed to supply our own bounds.\nFor this we use the Box2D type.\n\nIn this example we use the absolute mode to work with meshes in pixel space.\nWe create a Rectangle of 1 by 1, this will function as our pixel.\nNext we create a Box2D based on the resolution of the patch and use those as our bounds.\n\nTwo random nodes are used to create random x\/y positions and random colors.\nAA is disabled on the 2D Render node to make sure we get a crips result."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 993.1585693359375,
					"width": 2149.2001953125,
					"x": 35.57326126098632812,
					"y": 2010.9228515625
